      "side": 1,
      "message": "not really, I think __aligned would try to make sure that statically defined data is aligned as requested.\n\n__packed packs the fields together, as you mention *and* tells the compiler that this data might be misaligned, so the proper access assembler code is generated.\n\nAdding this patch fixed the unaligned exceptions the code was throwing before.",
